Chapter 5 – Solution Architecture
5.1 Architecture Overview

The MHMR Data Processing Framework is built on Microsoft Fabric Lakehouse using PySpark and Delta Tables. The solution follows a layered architecture to efficiently process daily data, detect changes, preserve historical records, maintain current-state snapshots, and provide comprehensive operational logging.

The framework is metadata-driven, allowing a common processing logic to be reused across hundreds of source tables while ensuring scalability, maintainability, and consistent execution.

The end-to-end data processing consists of the following major layers:

Source Systems
Raw Layer
Previous Raw Layer
Staging Layer
History Layer
Snapshot Layer
Logging Framework
Audit and Monitoring

Each layer has a clearly defined responsibility and works together to ensure reliable daily data processing.

